          %h3#relation_to_the_cobordism_hypothesis Relation to the cobordism hypothesis
          %blockquote
            %p check
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connective+spectrum"} connective spectrum
            is equivalently a grouplike
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+space"} E-∞ space
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Picard+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} Picard ∞-groupoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C0%29-category"} (∞,0)-category
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+dualizable+objects"} fully dualizable objects
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+hypothesis"} cobordism hypothesis
            this means that it is equipped with an
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(n)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-action"} ∞-action
            for all
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(n)
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/framed+manifold"} n-framings
            of the point in the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2Cn%29-category+of+cobordisms"} (∞,n)-category of cobordisms
            = succeed "-action" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(n)
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Lurie09"} Lurie 09, example 2.4.15
          %h3#relation_to_global_equivariant_stable_homotopy_theory Relation to global equivariant stable homotopy theory
          %p
            Since orthogonal spectra are by definition equipped with orthogonal group
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/actions"} actions
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+homotopy+theory"} equivariant homotopy theory
            “for all groups at once”, called
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+stable+homotopy+theory"} global stable homotopy theory
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+orthogonal+spectrum"} free orthogonal spectrum
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+ring+spectrum"} orthogonal ring spectrum
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+spectra"}> model structure on spectra
            ,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+smash+product+of+spectra"} symmetric monoidal smash product of spectra
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+spectrum"}> symmetric spectrum
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+symmetric+spectra"} model structure on symmetric spectra
            %li
              %p
                %strong> orthogonal spectrum
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+orthogonal+spectra"} model structure on orthogonal spectra
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-module"}> S-module
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+S-modules"} model structure on S-modules
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+equivariant+stable+homotopy+theory"} global equivariant stable homotopy theory
          %h2#references References
          %p Reviews include
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Knut Berg,
                %em Orthogonal spectra
                (
                %a{:href => "http://folk.uio.no/rognes/theses/orthogonal.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li#Malkiewich14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cary+Malkiewich"}> Cary Malkiewich
                , section 2.3 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The stable homotopy category
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://people.math.binghamton.edu/malkiewich/stable.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/MalkiewichStableHomotopyCategory.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p Lecture notes include
          %ul
            %li#Schwede12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Schwede"}> Stefan Schwede
                , chapter I, section 7.1 of
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Symmetric+spectra"} Symmetric spectra
                (2012)
            %li#Schwede14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Schwede"}> Stefan Schwede
                , section 1 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lectures+on+Equivariant+Stable+Homotopy+Theory"} Lectures on Equivariant Stable Homotopy Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.uni-bonn.de/people/schwede/equivariant.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            and (
            %a{:href => "#Schwede15"}> Schwede 15
            ) (take throughout
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℱ
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F} = \{1\}
            there to be the trivial family to restrict to the non-equivariant case).
          %p Orthogonal spectra were introduced around
          %ul
            %li#MMSS98a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Mandell"}> Michael Mandell
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"} Peter May
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Schwede"} Stefan Schwede
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brooke+Shipley"} Brooke Shipley
              = succeed "," do
                %em Diagram spaces, diagram spectra, and FSP’s
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uiuc.edu/K-theory/0319/"} KTheory:0319
          %p
            and their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalences"} Quillen equivalences
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories+of+spectra"} model categories of spectra
            were discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Mandell"}> Michael Mandell
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"} Peter May
                %em
                  Orthogonal spectra and
                  = succeed "-modules" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi S
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uiuc.edu/K-theory/0318/"}> K-theory:0318
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~may/PAPERS/mmLMSDec30.pdf"} pdf
            %li#MMSS98b
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Mandell"}> Michael Mandell
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"} Peter May
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Schwede"} Stefan Schwede
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brooke+Shipley"} Brooke Shipley
                = succeed "," do
